  '<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Client Profiles to Target</div>
<p><strong>DIY investors reacting to US market headlines:</strong> self directed investors who saw the sharp US tech selloff and assumed their Canadian heavy portfolio was equally exposed, without understanding the TSX''s different sector composition.</p>
<p><strong>Investors with concentrated single sector positions:</strong> those overweight in either energy or gold mining who have not had anyone separate the two distinct stories currently pressuring each sector.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Opening Line</div>
<div class="script-box">The TSX was essentially flat this week while US tech stocks sold off sharply, and underneath that calm headline number there are three separate sector stories worth understanding. Do you know how your portfolio''s Canadian versus US weighting affected what you experienced this week?</div>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Value Proposition</div>
<p>A DIY investor checking their portfolio against US market headlines this week likely saw a mismatch between what the news described and what their own statement showed, without understanding why. They are missing the structural explanation: the TSX''s heavier financials and energy weighting and lighter technology exposure made it less vulnerable to a chip stock driven selloff.</p>
<p>An advisor''s value is explaining not just what happened, but why the same global event produced different outcomes in different markets, and helping the client understand whether their specific sector exposure is positioned for the forces actually at work right now.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Discovery Questions</div>
<p>Were you surprised by how little your Canadian holdings moved this week compared to what you read about US markets?</p>
<p>Do you know your current sector weighting across financials, energy, and technology, and how that compares to the broader TSX composite?</p>
<p>Has anyone explained the difference between what is currently pressuring oil prices versus what is pressuring gold prices?</p>
<p>Are you currently positioned to benefit from regulatory tailwinds like this week''s bank capital changes, or are you unaware of how that affects your holdings?</p>
